WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:01.189 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  along the u.s canadian border the  trucker's blockade is slowly taking its  toll this paddle boarder is moving  faster than traffic  and as rebels and 18 wheelers demanding  an end to covet 19 restrictions continue  using their freedom convoy to block the  border on the canadian side the pain is  being felt on both sides  ford has stopped its auto assembly line  in windsor toyota has closed three  plants across ontario and general motors  is cutting shifts in michigan and those  closures threaten to reverberate  throughout the auto supply chain  despite the added time in traffic this  trucker says the demonstrators have a  point everybody  has the right you know to do whatever  you want you know  i want to die i want to die i don't care  i support them you know but i think it  kind of sucks you know all the traffic  here you know  on thursday the truckers opened another  front blocking all lanes on manitoba's  main crossing to north dakota and with  the ambassador bridge blocked from  detroit to windsor traffic on the  busiest land crossing in north america  is shut down entirely from the u.s to  canada and all but closed in the other  direction  trucks carrying everything from cattle  to car parts which under automaker's  just-in-time delivery system need to be  delivered within 48 hours to keep  assembly lines rolling have been  diverted to the crossing between port  huron michigan and the canadian city of  sarnia at the bluewater bridge these  trucks are getting across to canada but  wait times have been up to three hours  and traffic crawls and that's likely to  continue as long as the trucker's  blockade goes on and politicians seem  unwilling to crack down  canadian prime minister justin trudeau  insists canada will follow the science  not only are canadians tired of this  pandemic of  of the challenges we're facing but  they're also of course tired of the  restrictions tired of the rules tired of  the lockdowns that is understandable but  you know what helps lift restrictions  you know what helps move beyond  lockdowns  vaccinations  but some canadian provinces including  alberta and saskatchewan have eased  coveted rules and quebec and prince  edward island announced plans to do the  same  but with plans for a freedom convoy in  the u.s the truckers protests show no  sign of ending  john hendren al jazeera on the u.s  border with canada

